  "rate": "-15%",
  "parts": [
    {
      "module": "09",
      "part": "04",
      "revision": "m09p04-sap-m09-p04-p06-approved-review",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "cba464fab65d2f69eda48c02c99e829e62113fac4d01d09215064d295d01941e",
        "2": "cba464fab65d2f69eda48c02c99e829e62113fac4d01d09215064d295d01941e",
        "3": "cba464fab65d2f69eda48c02c99e829e62113fac4d01d09215064d295d01941e",
        "4": "e9212162838fe4ac6f9552e9cc40625045b60bd8ae41946b5affdefb86744fb5",
        "5": "e9212162838fe4ac6f9552e9cc40625045b60bd8ae41946b5affdefb86744fb5",
        "6": "e9212162838fe4ac6f9552e9cc40625045b60bd8ae41946b5affdefb86744fb5",
        "7": "e908dcd44019e92ed3af3ade73c42512cd250115958243ef993d1075617a6fc2",
        "8": "e908dcd44019e92ed3af3ade73c42512cd250115958243ef993d1075617a6fc2",
        "9": "e908dcd44019e92ed3af3ade73c42512cd250115958243ef993d1075617a6fc2",
        "10": "e908dcd44019e92ed3af3ade73c42512cd250115958243ef993d1075617a6fc2"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m09-s10-01",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "All three choices are for archives. What changes is how soon you can read the data. If a request needs the file in milliseconds, Glacier Instant Retrieval can serve it directly; budget for retrieval charges and a ninety-day minimum.",
          "text_sha256": "c1ecdb3acf78b79cbfe5e69f89a7376df0f8fb67e6430ecba0f134d497321fa2",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "c1ecdb3acf78b79cbfe5e69f89a7376df0f8fb67e6430ecba0f134d497321fa2",
          "asset_sha256": "cba464fab65d2f69eda48c02c99e829e62113fac4d01d09215064d295d01941e"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s10-02",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "If the job can wait, Glacier Flexible Retrieval can lower storage costs. Request a restore before reading. Choose a faster or cheaper retrieval option depending on when you need it; this class still has a ninety-day minimum.",
          "text_sha256": "1da8e9f4e91c912c69ac4fc3f53ceaacba5ac117cffb53a281ba963ad9abeda7",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "1da8e9f4e91c912c69ac4fc3f53ceaacba5ac117cffb53a281ba963ad9abeda7",
          "asset_sha256": "cba464fab65d2f69eda48c02c99e829e62113fac4d01d09215064d295d01941e"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s10-03",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "For a record you keep for years and can wait hours to recover, compare Deep Archive. Plan for a longer restore and a one-hundred-eighty-day minimum. Start with your recovery deadline, not the cheapest storage price.",
          "text_sha256": "61e25825c309cf719a63334d0918760d6241546ee92e23c10b01ccc29ce80a3f",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "61e25825c309cf719a63334d0918760d6241546ee92e23c10b01ccc29ce80a3f",
          "asset_sha256": "cba464fab65d2f69eda48c02c99e829e62113fac4d01d09215064d295d01941e"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s11-01",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "When access changes unpredictably, Intelligent-Tiering follows the object. It starts in Frequent Access. After thirty days without access it can move to Infrequent Access, and after ninety days total without access it can move to Archive Instant Access. That tier still serves reads immediately.",
          "text_sha256": "7c2defa379772cad64051d5be3a27d395f027b950fb4534ad6500915ee20f433",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "7c2defa379772cad64051d5be3a27d395f027b950fb4534ad6500915ee20f433",
          "asset_sha256": "e9212162838fe4ac6f9552e9cc40625045b60bd8ae41946b5affdefb86744fb5"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s11-02",
          "slide": 5,
          "text": "The optional archive tiers are different. You can set Archive Access after at least ninety days without access, or Deep Archive Access after at least one hundred eighty days. These are thresholds measured from inactivity, not a fresh countdown between the two boxes. Either tier requires a restore before reading.",
          "text_sha256": "276230d34a31153c762e8d235fb176dbab78719aed15dbbbdb08f75f88b7e586",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "276230d34a31153c762e8d235fb176dbab78719aed15dbbbdb08f75f88b7e586",
          "asset_sha256": "e9212162838fe4ac6f9552e9cc40625045b60bd8ae41946b5affdefb86744fb5"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s11-03",
          "slide": 6,
          "text": "Objects smaller than one hundred twenty-eight kilobytes stay in Frequent Access. S three does not monitor them for auto-tiering. Eligible objects incur the monitoring and automation charge, so check the size mix before you choose it.",
          "text_sha256": "5134557e4b84293bf9485faed819a5b4152606e64d440e503f3134ea8108be97",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "1cc91fcd2620026bb1acd2c1aa6fdbc8946bc87ce6922e189f1f18149ae327d5",
          "asset_sha256": "e9212162838fe4ac6f9552e9cc40625045b60bd8ae41946b5affdefb86744fb5"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s12-01",
          "slide": 7,
          "text": "A lifecycle rule acts on the version it targets. In a versioned bucket, expiring the current object can add a delete marker rather than erase the older data.",
          "text_sha256": "a192e6522f5229a9d329e9fa2524057796783f61e0d65683a1abd779a422f241",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "a192e6522f5229a9d329e9fa2524057796783f61e0d65683a1abd779a422f241",
          "asset_sha256": "e908dcd44019e92ed3af3ade73c42512cd250115958243ef993d1075617a6fc2"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s12-02",
          "slide": 8,
          "text": "The older copy now needs its own noncurrent-version action. You can transition that copy or expire it separately. Otherwise, hiding the current object does not stop storage charges on its older versions.",
          "text_sha256": "fbfc82184d3c20fdcd66cec3622c22af8a4c3f4dfeb99b94717b243929dc388a",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "fbfc82184d3c20fdcd66cec3622c22af8a4c3f4dfeb99b94717b243929dc388a",
          "asset_sha256": "e908dcd44019e92ed3af3ade73c42512cd250115958243ef993d1075617a6fc2"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s12-03",
          "slide": 9,
          "text": "When only an expired delete marker remains, the matching cleanup action can remove it. That is not the same as deleting an ordinary object version.",
          "text_sha256": "db51b110ce2ef95abfab597a98d170ef4f86444b09adf98547db2f5ec05cac20",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "db51b110ce2ef95abfab597a98d170ef4f86444b09adf98547db2f5ec05cac20",
          "asset_sha256": "e908dcd44019e92ed3af3ade73c42512cd250115958243ef993d1075617a6fc2"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s12-04",
          "slide": 10,
          "text": "A prefix or tag scopes the rule. Before applying it to all report versions, compare minimum storage durations, retrieval and metadata costs, and the transitions S three actually supports.",
          "text_sha256": "61dc55b34dbf74096737ed6353c8e8cfaea416723f5172486f3ff5127a4ac0e7",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "11e7165b782119dc717ddc88e3e5ff4fa1a9f8901d9b8726be2034a7252784b3",
          "asset_sha256": "e908dcd44019e92ed3af3ade73c42512cd250115958243ef993d1075617a6fc2"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "09",
      "part": "05",
      "revision": "m09p05-sap-m09-p04-p06-approved-review",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "a0e9e6fa69d8064da2aa1432f41b49fa367cccaa6fe8bebbf18262867ce4c322",
        "2": "a0e9e6fa69d8064da2aa1432f41b49fa367cccaa6fe8bebbf18262867ce4c322",
        "3": "a0e9e6fa69d8064da2aa1432f41b49fa367cccaa6fe8bebbf18262867ce4c322",
        "4": "ca4a2eee9d0f4901b16bcb15ad9fa894cf4837a7b62e399ade34fd2165afb830",
        "5": "ca4a2eee9d0f4901b16bcb15ad9fa894cf4837a7b62e399ade34fd2165afb830",
        "6": "ca4a2eee9d0f4901b16bcb15ad9fa894cf4837a7b62e399ade34fd2165afb830",
        "7": "b42b1bc561b63e3ea58dcae5c1bd7762eb822f3c18212e63f62618066ee0891f",
        "8": "b42b1bc561b63e3ea58dcae5c1bd7762eb822f3c18212e63f62618066ee0891f",
        "9": "b42b1bc561b63e3ea58dcae5c1bd7762eb822f3c18212e63f62618066ee0891f",
        "10": "b42b1bc561b63e3ea58dcae5c1bd7762eb822f3c18212e63f62618066ee0891f"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m09-s13-01",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "The source bucket is versioned. If a second team needs a copy that stays in the same Region, choose Same-Region Replication. That puts eligible object versions in a second bucket without crossing a regional boundary.",
          "text_sha256": "927f74930aa87ceca04faedf978cddc8abda0deacbb208c0715a95bb15becd82",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "927f74930aa87ceca04faedf978cddc8abda0deacbb208c0715a95bb15becd82",
          "asset_sha256": "a0e9e6fa69d8064da2aa1432f41b49fa367cccaa6fe8bebbf18262867ce4c322"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s13-02",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "If the requirement is a copy in another Region, choose Cross-Region Replication. Here the replica goes from US East one to US West two. Check data residency before making that choice.",
          "text_sha256": "3d6424d810b5737f62079d4ba440d45d40722692cf2a19996135bba0bdf01b41",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "3d6424d810b5737f62079d4ba440d45d40722692cf2a19996135bba0bdf01b41",
          "asset_sha256": "a0e9e6fa69d8064da2aa1432f41b49fa367cccaa6fe8bebbf18262867ce4c322"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s13-03",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Turn on versioning at both ends and give S three a role for the replication rule. For K M S-encrypted objects, configure the eligible source objects, destination key and permissions. The rule copies object versions; it does not duplicate the whole bucket configuration.",
          "text_sha256": "6ff077bc842117000586a87ccf0dba3e8b587fb1a8e68485a25320948ee7bfd1",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "27b592862ffdd9f96f83aa66c549071f32978e8a0028ed94e1332b7c414c455f",
          "asset_sha256": "a0e9e6fa69d8064da2aa1432f41b49fa367cccaa6fe8bebbf18262867ce4c322"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s14-01",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "A new report uploaded after the rule is enabled can replicate asynchronously. If the design needs predictable timing, S three Replication Time Control targets ninety-nine point nine nine percent of new objects within fifteen minutes under its service level agreement. Monitor for exceptions.",
          "text_sha256": "4c0c3a580b3c881cac0de7474feb822493c6716acf3b1b04c6add86c0ea6a6a8",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "22d9a8b08bf4cea5a9f9cc9932543dc1c2b87740e204390844134f27763cfaca",
          "asset_sha256": "ca4a2eee9d0f4901b16bcb15ad9fa894cf4837a7b62e399ade34fd2165afb830"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s14-02",
          "slide": 5,
          "text": "What about reports already in the bucket when you made the rule? Use Batch Replication to backfill eligible objects or repair gaps. The live timing commitment does not apply to that batch job.",
          "text_sha256": "989526293d006129a9cf5887b2f1cc24be14e285186e9bcc03722e194c9b87c9",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "989526293d006129a9cf5887b2f1cc24be14e285186e9bcc03722e194c9b87c9",
          "asset_sha256": "ca4a2eee9d0f4901b16bcb15ad9fa894cf4837a7b62e399ade34fd2165afb830"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s14-03",
          "slide": 6,
          "text": "For supported rules, you can opt in to replicating user-created delete markers. Permanently deleting a specific source version does not also delete that destination version. Test both cases rather than assuming the replica mirrors every deletion.",
          "text_sha256": "44fb912b0543e0225ba97dc92e23fcee4451c19297f501f72058433b92efcb3f",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "44fb912b0543e0225ba97dc92e23fcee4451c19297f501f72058433b92efcb3f",
          "asset_sha256": "ca4a2eee9d0f4901b16bcb15ad9fa894cf4837a7b62e399ade34fd2165afb830"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s15-01",
          "slide": 7,
          "text": "Suppose a new invoice should trigger processing. Select object creation. You can also subscribe to removals or supported restore events, but they mean something different to the consumer.",
          "text_sha256": "929d81fe6e2ea7698676f8483a25e80dbff2eb3d25bafcb4756808b46e669c49",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "929d81fe6e2ea7698676f8483a25e80dbff2eb3d25bafcb4756808b46e669c49",
          "asset_sha256": "b42b1bc561b63e3ea58dcae5c1bd7762eb822f3c18212e63f62618066ee0891f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s15-02",
          "slide": 8,
          "text": "To select invoice CSVs, use the prefix invoices slash and the suffix dot C S V. These are literal filters, not wildcard expressions.",
          "text_sha256": "193a245372ffba1bc908852939913afbf0c6965adc277930dc297ce7e00dbb7d",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "193a245372ffba1bc908852939913afbf0c6965adc277930dc297ce7e00dbb7d",
          "asset_sha256": "b42b1bc561b63e3ea58dcae5c1bd7762eb822f3c18212e63f62618066ee0891f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s15-03",
          "slide": 9,
          "text": "Send a matching event to a Lambda function, a standard S Q S queue, or a standard S N S topic, and authorize S three to deliver to that destination.",
          "text_sha256": "e4af775bdc5b93d41cc496147ffb92a03573212473a0e5b8642bd02ac24a6f71",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "9d276497e941598b17ec4e977f457daf79d4d0110e50b746ef541e988484081e",
          "asset_sha256": "b42b1bc561b63e3ea58dcae5c1bd7762eb822f3c18212e63f62618066ee0891f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s15-04",
          "slide": 10,
          "text": "Notifications are delivered at least once and can arrive out of order. If processing that invoice twice would post it twice, make the consumer recognize the already-processed event instead of assuming one notification means one transaction.",
          "text_sha256": "716f768ce9b3adbfdc19401fba62073d7ed846a066680cf59db424555da19518",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "716f768ce9b3adbfdc19401fba62073d7ed846a066680cf59db424555da19518",
          "asset_sha256": "b42b1bc561b63e3ea58dcae5c1bd7762eb822f3c18212e63f62618066ee0891f"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "09",
      "part": "06",
      "revision": "m09p06-sap-m09-p04-p06-approved-review",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "8ba94a674d400e16b6810258fa83bae4375e00b24f7cbc47c66ac2475dbe547b",
        "2": "8ba94a674d400e16b6810258fa83bae4375e00b24f7cbc47c66ac2475dbe547b",
        "3": "8ba94a674d400e16b6810258fa83bae4375e00b24f7cbc47c66ac2475dbe547b",
        "4": "8ba94a674d400e16b6810258fa83bae4375e00b24f7cbc47c66ac2475dbe547b",
        "5": "37ca4d9c86dbd60bdf8a4ce35067098edf819dc0743a526f5298df31ede5878c",
        "6": "37ca4d9c86dbd60bdf8a4ce35067098edf819dc0743a526f5298df31ede5878c",
        "7": "37ca4d9c86dbd60bdf8a4ce35067098edf819dc0743a526f5298df31ede5878c",
        "8": "37ca4d9c86dbd60bdf8a4ce35067098edf819dc0743a526f5298df31ede5878c",
        "9": "6b604e8368ae0d1f390f6eeb692f63d6a692c46722aa78c72214c59a189f6de3",
        "10": "6b604e8368ae0d1f390f6eeb692f63d6a692c46722aa78c72214c59a189f6de3",
        "11": "6b604e8368ae0d1f390f6eeb692f63d6a692c46722aa78c72214c59a189f6de3",
        "12": "6b604e8368ae0d1f390f6eeb692f63d6a692c46722aa78c72214c59a189f6de3",
        "13": "6b604e8368ae0d1f390f6eeb692f63d6a692c46722aa78c72214c59a189f6de3"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m09-s16-01",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Direct notifications can handle simple key filters. If you need event fields and multiple workflows, enable EventBridge on the bucket. S three sends its events to EventBridge, and the routing decisions happen on the bus.",
          "text_sha256": "807357721426ccd162a5e7961c26e88038703fec6a697dd5dd15fb98ef74f284",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "146923560d3e231d3b3df73e1748858d7b609001b74a2790d34d6832a3497c2e",
          "asset_sha256": "8ba94a674d400e16b6810258fa83bae4375e00b24f7cbc47c66ac2475dbe547b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s16-02",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "A rule can match the S three source, the event type, the bucket name and the object key. This example selects the named bucket and data slash file dot C S V, rather than reacting to every upload.",
          "text_sha256": "2de7c60480708b88d14961dea41391c6d49b79b916818978f9a3e5a313a64b28",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "c1936f5cd4910f083c3874622ecc558c64dea3da888d3eedca6295aef28183ba",
          "asset_sha256": "8ba94a674d400e16b6810258fa83bae4375e00b24f7cbc47c66ac2475dbe547b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s16-03",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "A match can start a Step Functions workflow, queue work in S Q S or invoke Lambda. Pick the target by what it should do with the event.",
          "text_sha256": "9f3bdb7e19ab67b4fb023fcdf5af36569c584d05fdc2a06093c79ef38a9edc48",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "8bca1e52bf885ef86135f8037304dd962709d34ecc9939583b7b9050ba2703ea",
          "asset_sha256": "8ba94a674d400e16b6810258fa83bae4375e00b24f7cbc47c66ac2475dbe547b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s16-04",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "Give EventBridge permission to reach each target. Set retries and, if needed, a dead-letter queue for failed deliveries. The consumer separately needs to handle duplicate deliveries without repeating the business action.",
          "text_sha256": "3527a12c44bcdf2d7118607bfa8e0a0826458e5f930b1d26bb69d48eadf10386",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "3527a12c44bcdf2d7118607bfa8e0a0826458e5f930b1d26bb69d48eadf10386",
          "asset_sha256": "8ba94a674d400e16b6810258fa83bae4375e00b24f7cbc47c66ac2475dbe547b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s17-01",
          "slide": 5,
          "text": "Images, logs and reports are prefixes: leading pieces of object keys, not physical folders. Parallel requests across useful partitioned prefixes let the application use more of S three's request capacity.",
          "text_sha256": "24f088540281d13c4cf4a7b284ecd95b0187b9e08e21f4e1bf82e18bb074ce5f",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "0dea087f7e054f50155d4514ee0df2dacca1d7beda18da79b828e44d48f61c5e",
          "asset_sha256": "37ca4d9c86dbd60bdf8a4ce35067098edf819dc0743a526f5298df31ede5878c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s17-02",
          "slide": 6,
          "text": "ay double-you ess documents at least thirty-five hundred write-type or fifty-five hundred get and HEAD requests per second per partitioned prefix. Those figures are a scaling baseline, not a fixed cap and not a guarantee for the whole application.",
          "text_sha256": "f188058587c9b9f4b258f5251b29ef6fe1dc7b535dcb622e96bdba62bbe65ad5",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "32d918b4755bdf6105e39cfe2841f9367a77a5ed4516817943f46bdebc76fe12",
          "asset_sha256": "37ca4d9c86dbd60bdf8a4ce35067098edf819dc0743a526f5298df31ede5878c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s17-03",
          "slide": 7,
          "text": "A sudden new request pattern can get a temporary five-oh-three Slow Down response while S three scales. Retry with backoff.",
          "text_sha256": "497864c4465a21b24153548ca4f7598035843067aee1eaa2cb881c1b1c2857be",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "11c84e96162c5621618db50c7d0bdc992badaff6420b5e485280818dc545244b",
          "asset_sha256": "37ca4d9c86dbd60bdf8a4ce35067098edf819dc0743a526f5298df31ede5878c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s17-04",
          "slide": 8,
          "text": "If requests remain slow, check client concurrency, the network and your K M S quotas rather than blaming the storage prefix alone.",
          "text_sha256": "51860bd85003e103c031bc02b013e08be332e507516447bc419d13ade25a5e90",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "0c53069db867cec15a7a7df40870fdf168dd6afdcc58e4b23eeb549a42ff76bd",
          "asset_sha256": "37ca4d9c86dbd60bdf8a4ce35067098edf819dc0743a526f5298df31ede5878c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s18-01",
          "slide": 9,
          "text": "For a large upload, start a multipart upload to get an upload ID. That ID lets the next requests add parts to the same transfer.",
          "text_sha256": "4206f5384b07915aa7a353f43f2c0d11954cf7c322cb43dd54bd2f6efb365c18",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "4206f5384b07915aa7a353f43f2c0d11954cf7c322cb43dd54bd2f6efb365c18",
          "asset_sha256": "6b604e8368ae0d1f390f6eeb692f63d6a692c46722aa78c72214c59a189f6de3"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s18-02",
          "slide": 10,
          "text": "Upload numbered parts in parallel and keep each returned E tag. If part two fails, retry part two with the same part number, not the entire upload.",
          "text_sha256": "4ef33c6a010d9349c36102dd1f29964eb305c634b151ab881d276c8c9a9107bd",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "9b7757b50663465b91ad742f6780340b1f8477c509c6bbac99679dac536002f6",
          "asset_sha256": "6b604e8368ae0d1f390f6eeb692f63d6a692c46722aa78c72214c59a189f6de3"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s18-03",
          "slide": 11,
          "text": "Send the ordered part numbers and E tags to Complete Multipart Upload. Only after that succeeds does S three assemble and expose the completed object.",
          "text_sha256": "7d84e5438fe2689aebdfb6dcd930f526d05ead32ad0b02f8d1843e9b508c1f10",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "6b7bde6ab4e0c0ae178beee802e5f5f1be38d3570a942636221f9f875dd753a7",
          "asset_sha256": "6b604e8368ae0d1f390f6eeb692f63d6a692c46722aa78c72214c59a189f6de3"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s18-04",
          "slide": 12,
          "text": "If you abandon the transfer, abort it so uploaded parts do not keep accumulating storage charges.",
          "text_sha256": "9551d7b5c67b72ce1c4f4fd3d81bc1e90c888ad40989f84338d1ea909718a13e",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "9551d7b5c67b72ce1c4f4fd3d81bc1e90c888ad40989f84338d1ea909718a13e",
          "asset_sha256": "6b604e8368ae0d1f390f6eeb692f63d6a692c46722aa78c72214c59a189f6de3"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09-s18-05",
          "slide": 13,
          "text": "Multipart is worth considering around a hundred megabytes, and it is required beyond the single-put limit. The final E tag is not necessarily an M D five hash, so use an appropriate checksum to verify integrity.",
          "text_sha256": "25c294b4e1a871bf3b46ec9c08d207b98e0c87753e0618962bbede5041529992",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "add26570a20bca7ae2dddc385db106821fcd2331258f26d2a837548d7cbeff47",
          "asset_sha256": "6b604e8368ae0d1f390f6eeb692f63d6a692c46722aa78c72214c59a189f6de3"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
